**Open** hemisphere (bowl, dome): $A = 2\pi r^{2}$, the curved surface only, with no flat face.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\usetikzlibrary{arrows.meta}
\draw (-1.7,0) arc (180:0:1.7);
\draw (-1.7,0) arc (180:360:1.7 and 0.5);
\draw (1.7,0) arc (0:180:1.7 and 0.5);
\fill (0,0) circle (1.2pt);
\draw[-{Stealth}] (0,0) -- (-20:1.7 and 0.5) node[midway,below,fill=white,inner sep=1pt] {$r$};
\node[below] at (0,-0.95) {open};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

**Closed** hemisphere (solid half-ball): $A = 2\pi r^{2} + \pi r^{2} = 3\pi r^{2}$, the curved surface plus the flat circular face.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\usetikzlibrary{arrows.meta}
\draw (-1.7,0) arc (180:0:1.7);
\draw (-1.7,0) arc (180:360:1.7 and 0.5);
\draw[dashed] (1.7,0) arc (0:180:1.7 and 0.5);
\fill (0,0) circle (1.2pt);
\draw[-{Stealth}] (0,0) -- (200:1.7 and 0.5) node[midway,below,fill=white,inner sep=1pt] {$r$};
\draw[-{Stealth}] (3.0,-0.95) -- (0.9,-0.18);
\node[right] at (3.0,-1.0) {flat face};
\node[below] at (0,-1.15) {closed};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

workedExamples.question_text:
An open hemispherical bowl has a radius of $5.5\,\mathrm{cm}$ and no flat circular face. Find its curved surface area, correct to 2 decimal places.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw (0,0) ellipse (1.8 and 0.5);
\draw (-1.8,0) arc[start angle=180,end angle=360,x radius=1.8,y radius=1.8];
\fill (0,0) circle (1.2pt);
\draw (0,0)--(1.8,0);
\path (0.9,0) node[above=2pt] {$5.5\,\mathrm{cm}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

An open hemispherical bowl has a diameter of $13\,\mathrm{cm}$ and no flat circular face. Find its curved surface area, correct to 2 decimal places.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw (0,0) ellipse (1.8 and 0.5);
\draw (-1.8,0) arc[start angle=180,end angle=360,x radius=1.8,y radius=1.8];
\draw (-1.8,0)--(1.8,0);
\path (0,0) node[above=2pt] {$13\,\mathrm{cm}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

